cff-version: 1.2.0
message: |
  If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: "alloylm: A self-contained framework for LLM training, inference, evaluation, and reinforcement learning"
abstract: |
  alloylm is a self-contained framework for large language model (LLM)
  training, inference, evaluation, and reinforcement learning. It provides
  end-to-end infrastructure including FSDP-based distributed training,
  SWA cache / sliding-window attention inference, tensor-parallel serving,
  MoE routing with partial expert loading, and an RL engine that supports
  rollout-routing replay for stabilizing MoE reinforcement learning.
